{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/333406-preservation-thread-stranger-transcendant-undertaking","id":333406,"title":"Preservation Thread: Stranger/Transcendant Undertaking","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-07T14:30:02-08:00","id":333406,"title":"Preservation Thread: Stranger/Transcendant Undertaking","content":"So this is some stuff that I managed to save from the old forum, six undertakings saved before the forum fell. If anyone can remember who wrote these, <i>tell me</i>, I want to make sure proper credit is given. <div align=\"center\"><b>Stranger</b><br /> <i>\u201cI\u2026 I need this. I need to be\u2026 complete.\u201d</i></div> <br /> In his own mind, the Stranger is defined less by what he is, and more by what he is not. For starters, he is not complete. When he looks in the mirror, he does not recognize the person staring back. His skin feels like a mask, his body a cage, confining the true self within. He is a beauty, a beast, a monster, trapped in weak, fallible flesh.<br /> <br /> The Stranger seeks to become whole. He seeks the transformative process, that which will bring forth his true self. He begins a quest for the formula, finding glances of the true self on the faces of others. He stakes his territory with a knife and a gun, seeking revelation in the fear and blood of his victims, trying to find that which will make him complete.<br /> <br /> A young man hires prostitutes, takes them to darkened hotel rooms, then slits their throats with a straight razor. As the blood pulses into his open mouth, he chokes on the bitter taste of copper and longs for the day when he becomes one of the undead, when the blood shall taste as sweet as pure ambrosia. A woman, seeking the strength of a man, kidnaps female-to-male transsexuals and performs autopsies on them, trying to find the form of the rebis, the alchemical marriage of the two genders. A brutish young orphan reads of the nephilim, the abandoned children of treacherous angels, and defiles church altars with the bodies of their priests in an unholy black mass, hoping that the Grigori will see his deeds and assume him into the fold.<br /> <br /> <b>Background</b>: The Stranger\u2019s desire for completion is rooted first and foremost in the denial of his own self. He is not a person \u2013 at least, not as he is now. What he is is weak, and humble, and worthless. It is only through adopting the persona of another that he can come to terms with his own existence and feel like he is more than a shadow on the wall.<br /> <br /> Usually, a Stranger reaches such depths of self-loathing through a period of great trauma. Perhaps he loses his entire family in a freak accident, and blames himself for some perceived weakness that prevented him from coming to their aid. Maybe his childhood was characterized by abuse from a guardian, wherein he was attacked for being a \u201cfreak.\u201d He views himself as a mockery of existence, and wants to find out why other people can just be who they are so easily. The quest to get under another person\u2019s skin may involve him slicing it off and wearing it as a mask.<br /> <br /> A Stranger may begin their career as a hunter out of a desire to get closer to his chosen targets. His research into lycanthropy myths may prove invaluable to a cell that spends their time tracking down werewolves who feed on human flesh\u2026 at least, until his comrades find the bodies, missing pieces of skin that he\u2019s taken to cure into a wolfskin belt of his own. Similarly, a Stranger may be a hunter who has experienced real loss at the hands of monsters. When a partner in his cell is torn to pieces at the claws of a raging vampire, he may wish to claim the heart of the creature\u2019s power for revenge. But the more he finds himself trying to match the monster, the more he comes to empathize its point of view.<br /> <br /> A Stranger is a versatile being, willing to do anything to accomplish his goal. Their Attributes and Skills depend as much upon their quarry as themselves. A man who hunts young women who idle into the forest after dark in an attempt to become a werewolf will favor Physical Attributes and Skills such as Survival and Animal Ken, while a pretty young thing who desires to become the lamia and drive men to ruin will focus on Social Attributes and Skills such as Expression and Persuasion. All Strangers have a strong head for Skills such as Academics, Medicine, Occult, or Science \u2013 they wish to understand their other self, inside and out.<br /> <br /> <b>Inspirations</b>: Martin (<i>Martin</i>), Francis Dolarhyde (<i>Red Dragon</i>), Hedy Carlson (<i>Single White Female</i>), Buffalo Bill (<i>The Silence of the Lambs</i>)<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes</b>: Intelligence, Resolve, Dexterity or Stamina<br /> <br /> <b>Undertaking Skills</b>: Academics, Animal Ken, Investigation, Larceny, Medicine, Streetwise, Survival, Weaponry<br /> <br /> <b>Talent \u2013 Dreams of the Other</b>: The Stranger seeks with all his will to become the persona he holds in his heart. His heart sings as he approaches the quarry, and when the blade finds home, he exults in the revelation that comes with it. When he pursues a target directly related to his goal of apotheosis, he has the option to risk Willpower on the roll, just like a hunter (see Hunter: the Vigil). Furthermore, if he is successful in his hunt and manages to \u201clearn\u201d from his target, he gains a +2 to all rolls to risk Willpower for the next scene. The glory of the revelation fades soon after, however, and he must begin his hunt for perfection again.<br /> <br /> <b>Frailty \u2013 No Heart But Another\u2019s</b>: At his very core, the Stranger seeks to become something else because he has no true sense of identity. His real name is an alias, his face is a mask, and his words are always lies. When the Stranger makes an Expression, Persuasion, or Socialize roll, he makes it at a -3 penalty at all times. If he is pursuing a quarry, he can spend Willpower to offset the penalty and even risk Willpower to ensure great success, but in all other cases, the Stranger\u2019s true emptiness shines through.<br /> <br /> <b>VASCU Case Study: The Tithe-Keeper</b><br /> <i>From the files of VASCU forensic psychologist Sarah Kepler</i><br /> <br /> <i>When I finally had the chance to sit down for an interview with Jessica Casey, I found a woman very different from what I had expected. Her medical history had indicated a history of manic-depressive behavior, but that was nothing compared to the woman who walked like one of the condemned into the interview area. The scars of past suicide attempts marked her wrists -- one of the cuts still appeared fresh -- and her eyes... her eyes were always clouded. Like she was on the verge of tears.<br /> <br /> &quot;They won't come for me,&quot; was the first thing she said to me, and she didn't want to let it go. With enough poking, I began to get her to talk about her past. Her mother had always told her fairy tales before going to bed, but that had been before the accident. Afterwards, she ended up in the possession of her uncle Francis, who had subjected her to physical and emotional abuse for six years before child services had noticed. Every time I compelled a fact from her, she ended the sentence with, &quot;They won't come for me.&quot;<br /> <br /> The next session, I began by asking her who &quot;they&quot; were, and if they'd had anything to do with the children -- seven young boys and girls, all of whom had been in Casey's care, all of whose seemingly unmarred bodies were found in forests secreted away under trees and in rings of mushrooms. When I broached the topic, she began to break down crying, and said that &quot;they&quot; couldn't hear her here, due to the iron in the walls. She curled up on the floor and cried for her mother -- her <b>true</b> mother, Queen Mab of the Faeries -- until the guards came to take her back to the cell.<br /> <br /> Jessica Casey escaped from her cell on November 1st, 2008, and her absence was not noted until cell inspections that night. Her true whereabouts are still unknown.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T14:32:06-08:00","id":333419,"title":"","content":"<b>Transcendent</b><br /> <i>\u201cBehold my glory, and despair.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> The only thing more dangerous than a man who kills for his ideals is one who has accomplished them and sees no reason to stop. Through the study of blood, flesh, and death, the Stranger becomes something more than human. They have unlocked the secrets of apotheosis, accomplished their dream, and freed themselves from the cage of meat and bone. They have become Transcendent, and nothing is beyond their limit.<br /> <br /> Some green VASCU agents question why a Stranger would keep killing once he\u2019s attained his own twisted sense of perfection. Those who deal in the cases of the Transcendent know that mere perfection is never enough. For the slasher, the body has gone from cage to altar. It is a wild fire, a mad god, an engine of destruction, something both beautiful and terrible to behold. The Transcendent demands adoration, and like an Old Testament God, is fully willing to strike down the blasphemous to secure the worthy.<br /> <br /> The worst part of dealing with one of the Transcendent is that they serve as testament to an uncomfortable truth \u2013 <i>they were right</i>. What a forensic psychologist might dismiss as delusion or psychosis is proven to be dark alchemy, a precise formula that gave them all their heart\u2019s desires. Hunters who face down Transcendents carry with them tales of a man who took a shotgun blast to his bare chest and kept charging, a woman who could burn a man\u2019s skin with just a touch, and a delusional prophet whose very words were honey. There is <i>something</i> out there that is willing to reward slashers for their bitter deeds, and as long as there is murder in the world, it will <i>always</i> have a supplicant.<br /> <br /> <b>Background</b>: Many serial killers have a superiority complex. They honestly believe that they are above the rest of humanity, that the average man means as much to them as the average cattle. The Transcendent not only follows this ethos, but adheres to it with a steely certainty; he <i>knows</i> for a fact that he is more than mortal.<br /> <br /> While the Transcendent is most often the \u201cevolved\u201d state of a Stranger who has discovered the truth of his Undertaking, it\u2019s possible for a slasher to instantly reach the state of accomplishment in a moment of dreadful revelation. Perhaps he finds a horrible secret of the universe written in a dusty tome, or discovers his bloodline is traced to an ancient clan of monsters. Those members of VASCU who know about the Lucifuge look upon the Children of the Seventh Generation with distrust; when you believe yourself to be a child of Hell, it\u2019s only a matter of degrees until you\u2019re doing the Devil\u2019s will.<br /> <br /> Like the Stranger, the character creation for a Transcendent is flexible and depends greatly on the focus of the rebirth. The man who desires to become a Faustian devil will focus his interests in a different direction than the woman who wishes to embody the wrath of the Furies. Another important factor in creating a Transcendent is that they are, at their very core, malleable. Their Talent lies in adopting the traits of their new self; they can be whatever they want, as long as it fits their ethos.<br /> <br /> <b>Inspirations</b>: Serial Killer X (<i>Condemned: Criminal Origins</i>), Edgar Reese/Azazel (<i>Fallen</i>), The Metal Fetishist (<i>Tetsuo the Iron Man</i>), SID 6.7 (<i>Virtuosity</i>)<br /> <br /> <b>Attribute</b>: Intelligence, Resolve, Dexterity or Stamina<br /> <br /> <b>Undertaking Skills</b>: Academics, Animal Ken, Intimidation, Investigation, Larceny, Medicine, Occult, Streetwise, Survival, Weaponry<br /> <br /> <b>Talent \u2013 Malleable Self</b>: The Transcendent appears mortal, but can call forth his true self at will. Once per scene, the Transcendent can spend a point of Willpower and roll Resolve + Composure. He cannot risk Willpower on this roll, or spend Willpower to increase the roll itself. Once the roll is made, the Transcendent can spend successes on changes to their form:<br /> <br /> -+1 to Skill (1 success per dot)<br /> -+1 to Attribute (3 successes per dot)<br /> -Iron Stamina Merit(1 success per dot)<br /> -Striking Looks Merit (1 success for 2 dots, 2 successes for 4 dots)<br /> -Natural Weaponry (1 success per +1L; 1 extra success to make damage elemental)<br /> -Natural Armor (2 successes per level)<br /> -Healing damage (1 success per level of Bashing, 2 successes per level of Lethal, 4 successes per level of Aggravated)<br /> <br /> These changes <i>must</i> relate to the form they have adopted; the Storyteller has final say on whether or not an adaptation is thematically related.<br /> <br /> <b>Frailty \u2013 Only Human</b>: The Transcendent may believe he has grown beyond the bonds of humanity, but in many ways, he is still fettered to the corpse of his old self. His weakness lies in being reminded that he is still mortal, and his \u201ctrue self\u201d is mere decoration added to human clay. Like with his Talent, the Transcendent\u2019s Frailty is entirely thematic. A white supremacist self-proclaimed <i>ubermensch</i> may find a black hunter has gotten the upper hand in a fist fight, whereas a woman who patterns herself after the Great Whore of Babylon and delights in driving holy men to ruination may find sympathy at the hands of a member of the Long Night.<br /> <br /> When the Transcendent is confronted with evidence of his old self and human failings, the mask cracks instantly. All benefits derived from their Talent vanish automatically, leaving his with just his natural aptitudes. Furthermore, crushing doubt overtakes the Transcendent as he struggles with the knowledge that he isn\u2019t as perfect as he believes; as a result, he takes a -2 penalty to <i>all</i> rolls for the remainder of the scene. Most Transcendents flee from such confrontations, usually isolating themselves until they\u2019ve managed to suppress the crushing realization\u2026 and swear revenge on those who brought forth their flaws.<br /> <br /> <b>VASCU Case Study: Lilith</b><br /> <i>From the files of anthropologist Michael Ntuze<br /> I first met Dr. Lillian Carver three years into my fellowship at the Smithsonian, when I was leading a program into the search for \u201cMitochondrial Eve\u201d \u2013 the common ancestor of all humanity. She came to us with a laundry list of accolades: summa cum laude at Georgetown, graduate study at Oxford, a Pell Grant at 25\u2026 she certainly knew the territory. She had spent years on research expeditions in Africa, following the trail of anthropological studies. We did question the fact that her studies had taken her to Nigeria, Sudan, and Zimbabwe during periods of civil unrest and genocide; her only explanation was that she \u201cstudied with the best.\u201d<br /> <br /> From the start, there seemed something\u2026 odd about Dr. Carver. She always seemed withdrawn, and never joined us outside of work. I had known my share of eccentrics during my stay in academia, and merely attributed it to personal quirks. Then I heard stories of the men who turned up in motel rooms on I-495, subjected to extensive surgery while they were still alive. Around this time, I began to notice a change in Dr. Carver \u2013 she seemed more vivacious, more alluring, and even fervid at times.<br /> <br /> When she failed to show up for work for three days, I took one of the slides from her worktable to the police on a whim \u2013 it had come from one of the men on I-495. They came to our lab and found a manifest on her computer, proclaiming herself to be \u201cthe outlier,\u201d \u201cthe betrayed mother of humanity.\u201d The letter was signed, \u201cLilith.\u201d<br /> <br /> Every few months, I receive a new slide from her. I never test it.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T18:53:43-08:00","id":333658,"title":"","content":"Considering that slashers can have endowments, belong to or form compacts or conspiracies, use tactics, and when a hunter switches to a slasher the only thing they lose according to canon is their professional training, I'd assume that slashers can risk willpower as well. <br /> <br /> At least, former hunters would seem to retain the ability, and former hunters and non former hunter slashers don't seem to have any mechanical differences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T12:00:45-08:00","id":334404,"title":"","content":"I like these guys.<br /> <br /> I have two questions, though.<br /> <br /> One, do you think it would accurately represent the killer from the film Taking Lives? And with this undertaking, do you think it would be more appropriate for the sample Slasher John Smith, from the Slashers book? He is listed as a charmer, but sounds a lot like a Stranger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T13:19:25-08:00","id":334497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/333406-preservation-thread-stranger-transcendant-undertaking?p=333658#post333658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that slashers can have endowments, belong to or form compacts or conspiracies, use tactics, and when a hunter switches to a slasher the only thing they lose according to canon is their professional training, I'd assume that slashers can risk willpower as well.</div> </div> </div> </div> I would too.<br /> <br /> I generally assume that Hunters, Slashers and Cultists can all risk willpower. Note that those are not discreet categories:<br /> <br /> Hunter - sees through the self imposed lie that the supernatural does not exist.<br /> Slasher - a specific kind of serial killer<br /> Cultists - a member of a cult.<br /> <br /> You can be all three. (A cultist who worships an active and clearly supernatural deity through human sacrafice)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T07:35:04-08:00","id":335160,"title":"","content":"I never really thought about cultists risking willpower. Not that I see any real reason why not, at their most impressive a cultist would have some dread powers, but heck hunters can have those too. <br /> <br /> Hmm, now I'm wondering why Witchfinders didn't include cult talk, witchcraft, cults, they go together like peanut butter and chocolate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T10:58:10-08:00","id":335324,"title":"","content":"Would the Transcendent self really be that shocking to the average Hunter? I mean, they deal with freaking Werewolves and Vampires(I admit, VASCU perhaps less), who have far more mechanical advantages. <br /> <br /> Granted, they do get auto successes, so there's that. <br /> <br /> <br /> Otherwise, the Stranger and Transcendent are excellent. They fill in a much needed niche, as now one can fully role-play out Silence of the Lambs, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T19:28:23-08:00","id":1033097,"title":"","content":"/Unless I'm reading this wrong, this sounds like a great possibility for antagonististic fetches. Whether the truth has been revealed to them or they just always felt that they were not whole in some way, the idea of searching for completion is very fetch-like. So, are fetches considered human enough to have the capacity to become Slashers by RAW? Cause I would totally love to see this used in a Changeling game. Congratulations, you got your life back without killing your fetch by informing him of his true nature! Except now you just created a Slasher whose either going after his/your family members and/or other Changelings (local Courts are not going to like you) in a desperate quest to become whole. All because you convinced him he was broken and incomplete so you could go home and try to pretend your durance never happened. Mission accomplished!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T02:16:28-08:00","id":1033924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/333406-preservation-thread-stranger-transcendant-undertaking?p=1033097#post1033097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">/Unless I'm reading this wrong, this sounds like a great possibility for antagonististic fetches. Whether the truth has been revealed to them or they just always felt that they were not whole in some way, the idea of searching for completion is very fetch-like. So, are fetches considered human enough to have the capacity to become Slashers by RAW? Cause I would totally love to see this used in a Changeling game. Congratulations, you got your life back without killing your fetch by informing him of his true nature! Except now you just created a Slasher whose either going after his/your family members and/or other Changelings (local Courts are not going to like you) in a desperate quest to become whole. All because you convinced him he was broken and incomplete so you could go home and try to pretend your durance never happened. Mission accomplished!</div> </div> </div> </div>If memory serves Fetches count as sleepwalkers, and that's there only difference between themselves and normal humans. So yes, I'd say a Fetch can indeed become a Slasher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T03:01:45-08:00","id":1033935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/333406-preservation-thread-stranger-transcendant-undertaking?p=1033924#post1033924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If memory serves Fetches count as sleepwalkers, and that's there only difference between themselves and normal humans. So yes, I'd say a Fetch can indeed become a Slasher.</div> </div> </div> 